<Base title="Affiliate disclosure" description="Which links on TheTravelFact can pay a commission, and which slots are not links yet.">
  <article class="shell page prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclosure</p>
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p>Updated 14 November 2026.</p>
    <p>Some outbound links can earn a commission. They are marked <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>. A commission does not change the climate table or the cited facts.</p>
    <h2>Amazon</h2>
    <p>The travel-adapter button is an Amazon search with associate tag <code>thetravelfact-20</code>. If you buy through it, we may earn a commission. It is a search, not a product we tested.</p>
    <h2>Hotels and tours</h2>
    <p>The sheet reserves slots for Viator, Expedia, Booking.com, and Travelpayouts. Those program IDs are empty. The slots are labels, not links, and they are not affiliate links until an ID is added and this page says so.</p>
    <h2>Display ads</h2>
    <p>Each sheet has an empty slot where a display ad could go later. No ad script is on the site today.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
